From: MacGameVideoFix <https://github.com/MathiasKowoll/MacGameVideoFix>
Subject: [PATCH] ntoskrnl.exe: refresh a device's hardware and compatible ids on every enumeration

WHERE THIS CAME FROM

MacGameVideoFix's own series, mgvf-NNNN, written on 2026-09-08, the third of
three for the same fault. Nothing in it is specific to this project.

THE FAULT

With mgvf-0002 winebus reports a BTHENUM compatible id for a Bluetooth pad, and
with mgvf-0003 CM_Get_Parent hands hidapi the bus PDO to read it from. Measured
with a +setupapi trace: Steam asked for the parent, got it, read its
CompatibleIds -- and still logged "bluetooth 0". The value it read was the old
one. enumerate_new_device writes SPDRP_HARDWAREID and SPDRP_COMPATIBLEIDS only
inside install_device_driver, which runs only when the Enum key has no driver
yet: the first time a device is ever seen. Every later boot keeps the record of
that first boot, whatever the bus says now.

THE CHANGE

enumerate_new_device asks the bus for its hardware and compatible ids on every
enumeration and writes them, before the driver question. install_device_driver
still writes them too on a first install; writing them twice then is harmless.
That is Windows's behaviour: the PnP manager keeps these properties current.

---
--- a/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/pnp.c
+++ b/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/pnp.c
@@ -434,6 +434,25 @@
         ExFreePool( id );
     }
 
+    /* MGVF: the hardware and compatible ids are the bus's answer of today, not
+     * of the day the device was first seen. They were written only by
+     * install_device_driver, i.e. once, so a bus that learned to report more
+     * (winebus naming the Bluetooth transport) was masked by the record of an
+     * earlier boot for as long as the key lived. Windows keeps these current
+     * on every enumeration; so does this now. */
+    if (!get_device_id( device, BusQueryHardwareIDs, &id ) && id)
+    {
+        SetupDiSetDeviceRegistryPropertyW( set, &sp_device, SPDRP_HARDWAREID, (BYTE *)id,
+                sizeof_multiszW( id ) * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+        ExFreePool( id );
+    }
+    if (!get_device_id( device, BusQueryCompatibleIDs, &id ) && id)
+    {
+        SetupDiSetDeviceRegistryPropertyW( set, &sp_device, SPDRP_COMPATIBLEIDS, (BYTE *)id,
+                sizeof_multiszW( id ) * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+        ExFreePool( id );
+    }
+
     if (need_driver && !install_device_driver( device, set, &sp_device ) && !caps.RawDeviceOK)
     {
         ERR("Unable to install a function driver for device %s.\n", debugstr_w(device_instance_id));
